Acts: ["Hilltop", "Bridge", "Ravine"]
States: ["North", "South"]
Probabilities: {"North": 0.5, "South": 0.5}
Payoffs: {"Hilltop": {"North": 20, "South": 8}, "Bridge": {"North": 12, "South": 7}, "Ravine": {"North": 1, "South": 5}}

Acts: G1, G2, G3, G4; States: Red (p=1/3), Black (p=?), Yellow (p=?);
Payoffs: G1|Red=100, G1|Black=0, G1|Yellow=0; G2|Red=0, G2|Black=100, G2|Yellow=0; G3|Red=100, G3|Black=0, G3|Yellow=100; G4|Red=0, G4|Black=100, G4|Yellow=100;
Preference implications: G1>G2 ⇒ p(Black)<1/3; G4>G3 ⇒ p(Black)>1/3 – contradiction.

Acts: [Accept, Reject]; States: HH (p=0.25), HT (p=0.25), TH (p=0.25), TT (p=0.25);
Payoffs: Accept|HH=+5, Accept|TT=+5, Accept|HT=‑4, Accept|TH=‑4;
Unconditional EV = (+5+5‑4‑4)/4 = +0.5;
Event A = ‘at least one H’ → outcomes {HH, HT, TH}, P(win|A)=1/3, EV|A = (5‑4‑4)/3 = –1;
Event B = ‘at least one T’ → outcomes {TT, HT, TH}, P(win|B)=1/3, EV|B = (5‑4‑4)/3 = –1;
A and B overlap on {HT, TH} (the losing outcomes).

Acts = {Lottery, Insurance, SurePrize, GambleEscape}; States = {LowP_Gain, LowP_Loss, HighP_Gain, HighP_Loss};
Utility = Σ π(p_i)·v(x_i) where v(x) is S‑shaped and π(p) overweights p<0.1, underweights p>0.9.
Decision rule: choose act with maximal Σ π·v.

players: ["Brother Tomas", "Brother Lucian"]
strategies: ["Cooperate (C)", "Defect (D)"]
payoffs: {"(C,C)": [3, 3], "(C,D)": [0, 5], "(D,C)": [5, 0], "(D,D)": [1, 1]}

Players: [Lira, Kade]; Strategies: [Tit‑for‑Tat (TFT), Always Defect (AllD), Always Cooperate (AllC), Grim Trigger]; Payoffs per round: (C,C)=(3,3), (C,D)=(0,5), (D,C)=(5,0), (D,D)=(1,1);
TFT vs TFT over n rounds: each receives 3n;
TFT vs AllD: round 1 → (0,5); rounds 2‑n → (1,1) each;
Cooperation sustainable when δ > (T‑R)/(T‑P) = 0.5.

Players: [Merchants]; Strategies: [Haggle (proportion p), Fair Trade (proportion 1-p)];
Profit functions: E(H)=5-7p, E(F)=3-3p;
Average profit: \bar{f}=p·E(H)+(1-p)·E(F);
Replicator equation for Haggle: dp/dt = p (E(H)-\bar{f});
Equilibrium when E(H)=E(F) → 5-7p = 3-3p → p* = 0.5; Stability: if p>0.5, E(F)>E(H) → p decreases; if p<0.5, E(H)>E(F) → p increases.

Acts = {G1,G2,G3,G4}; States = {Red (p=1/3), Black (p=?), Yellow (p=?)};
Payoffs: G1|Red=100, G1|Black=0, G1|Yellow=0;
         G2|Red=0, G2|Black=100, G2|Yellow=0;
         G3|Red=100, G3|Black=0, G3|Yellow=100;
         G4|Red=0, G4|Black=100, G4|Yellow=100;
Preference G1>G2 ⇒ p(Black)<1/3; Preference G4>G3 ⇒ p(Black)>1/3; contradiction.

Players: [Poacher, Ranger];
Strategies:
  Poacher = {Enter, Stay Out};
  Ranger = {Accommodate, Fight};
Payoffs:
  (Enter, Accommodate) = (2, 2);
  (Enter, Fight) = (0, 0);
  (Stay Out, Fight) = (1, 3);
  (Stay Out, Accommodate) = (1, 3);
Subgame at Ranger node after Enter: Accommodate (2) > Fight (0).
SPE: (Enter, Accommodate) survives; (Stay Out, Fight) is eliminated because Fight is not optimal in the subgame.
